class Mod

// The base class of every Endless Sky mod. A mod extends it, overrides the hooks
// it needs, and is built into one JavaScript file (`npm run build` in the mod
// SDK, or `tools/dado-mods.sh mod <dir>` in the loader's repository):
//
//     class ShieldWall extends es.Mod
//
//     import "imports:sdk/es"
//
//     string name():
//         return "shield wall"
//
//     void on_step(es.Game game, int step):
//         if every(step, 1.0):
//             for i in player_ships(game):
//                 game.set_shields(i, game.shields(i) + 10.0)
//
// This class is compiled into each mod, so its helpers cost no call into the
// game. Hooks run on the game's main thread while the simulation is paused; a
// hook that throws is reported once and switched off for that mod.

// The mod API this mod was built against (the SDK's MOD_API): for information.
// Do not override; to say which API the mod needs, override min_api.
int api_version():
    return MOD_API

// (Mod API 10.) The oldest mod API this mod runs on: a loader refuses the mod
// only when this is newer than the API it speaks. The default, 1, runs it on
// every loader that knows min_api; a mod that cannot do without a newer call
// returns that call's API version. For a feature it can do without, check
// Game.has("<feature>") instead, so the mod still runs on an older game.
int min_api():
    return 1

// The mod's name, used by `log`. Override it.
string name():
    return "unnamed mod"

// Called once, after the mod loads and before its first step.
void on_load(Game game):
    return

// Called every engine step (60 per second) while the player is flying and the game is not paused.
void on_step(Game game, int step):
    return

// Called once for each new day (days since the epoch), before on_enter on a
// jump. Days pass when the player jumps or takes off.
void on_day(Game game, int day):
    return

// Called when the player arrives in a system (its true name), and once when
// the mod starts in flight. Spawn ships the player should find here.
void on_enter(Game game, string system):
    return

// Called when the player clicks this mod's planet-screen button (see
// Game.planet_button). Game.panel_open works here.
void on_planet_button(Game game):
    return

// Called when the player clicks a button on this mod's panel.
void on_panel(Game game, int button):
    return

// (Mod API 5.) Whether this mod's outfitter button (see Game.outfitter_button)
// is enabled, for the outfitter's selected `outfit` ("" for none) and ships
// (Game.outfitter_ship). Runs every frame the outfitter is drawn: keep it quick.
bool can_outfitter(Game game, string outfit):
    return true

// (Mod API 5.) Called when the player clicks this mod's outfitter button.
// Game.confirm works here.
void on_outfitter(Game game, string outfit):
    return

// (Mod API 5.) Called when the player clicks OK in a dialog this mod opened
// with Game.confirm, with the token it gave.
void on_confirm(Game game, int token):
    return

// (Mod API 6.) Called when the player clicks a row of this mod's panel table
// (see Game.panel_columns); `row` is its index, in the order the rows were added.
void on_panel_row(Game game, int row):
    return

// (Mod API 7.) Called when the player clicks a column heading of this mod's
// table on its full screen (Game.screen_open); `column` counts from 0.
void on_panel_header(Game game, int column):
    return

// (Mod API 6.) Called when the player answers a Game.ask_number dialog with OK.
void on_number(Game game, int token, int value):
    return

// (Mod API 10.) Called just before the game writes the pilot to a file: when
// the player takes off, quits while landed or opens the load panel, for the
// autosave when the player accepts a mission marked `autosave` (which may be
// in flight), and when a conversation starts (a save during it writes that
// moment). What the mod writes with Game.set_data now goes into that file, so
// a mod may keep its state in memory and write it here only. Queries,
// set_data, conditions and stock work; panels and dialogs do not, and there is
// no ship snapshot even in flight (ship_count is 0). It may run twice for one
// save. What it posts with notify arrives after the save, and is lost when the
// player then loads another pilot or quits.
void on_save(Game game):
    return

// (Mod API 10.) Called once when the player makes or loads another pilot (and
// when the mods start with one): after on_load, before any on_day, on_enter or
// on_step for that pilot. Reset what the mod keeps in memory for the last pilot
// here, and read this one's saved data. Panels and dialogs do not work here.
void on_pilot_loaded(Game game):
    return

// (Mod API 10.) A notification another mod posted with Game.notify, named
// `name`, which this mod listens for (Game.listen); `sender` is the mod that
// posted it, as the game recorded it. Panels and dialogs do not work here.
void on_notification(Game game, string name, string payload, string sender):
    return

// Write a line to the game's log, prefixed with the mod's name.
void log(Game game, string text):
    game.log(name() + ": " + text)

// True once every `seconds` of game time, for spreading work out over steps.
bool every(int step, float seconds):
    int period = int(seconds * 60.0)
    if period < 1:
        return true
    return step % period == 0

// The indices of the player's ships in the current system that are not disabled.
[]int player_ships(Game game):
    []int out = []
    for i in 0..<game.ship_count():
        if game.is_player(i) && !game.is_disabled(i):
            out.append(i)
    return out
